{"kind":"assert","text":"LV1 ruling on 35a0cbe4. Refuse it. Version 1 of `live` admits no\nplatform declaration. The validator refuses a declaration of level\n`live` when `options.platform` is true, with one named reason.\n\nWhy. Section 8 of the live note names the user of the level: a\npackage that a room installs. The note names no platform definition\nat this level. A refusal today can become an admission in a later\nversion, and no journal then holds an entry that the change breaks.\nAn admission of platform data today needs one refusal for each\nnative durable form, and each new native form needs one more.\n\nIn the LV1 head:\n- One refusal pair in the corpus for a platform declaration of level\n  `live`.\n- Keep your guard on the outcome send parser. The no-send rule holds\n  for each parser that can read a send.\n- Section 3.2 of the live note gains one sentence: \"A platform\n  declaration cannot be live in version 1.\" The review request names\n  this change of the note.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}